# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# Plans of cuFFT for more grids than the 8 of the table the runtime had
# (#323): frame evaluators of three grids with tunable charges in one
# process, four plans a grid in mixed precision, the case of the issue, and
# six in all in double. Before the fix the mixed run ended the process at
# the ninth plan ("mdrt: too many grids of FFT", status -6).
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_fft_plans.py %S/Inputs Mixed | FileCheck %s -DMODE=Mixed
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_fft_plans.py %S/Inputs Double | FileCheck %s -DMODE=Double
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: amber at 64 points: finite energy and gradients
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: amber at 128 points: finite energy and gradients
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: water at 32 points: finite energy and gradients
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the first evaluator again, after 3 grids: the same bits
# CHECK: fft plans passed
